  "description": "POV: you get a gift card and toss it in a drawer. See where the money sits.\n\nSources:\n- Bankrate press release, Sept 23, 2024 (survey by YouGov, fieldwork Aug 19-21, 2024): https://www.bankrate.com/f/102997/x/c53caa68d4/gift-card-survey-press-release.pdf\n- Bankrate: Survey on unused gift cards (2024): https://www.bankrate.com/credit-cards/news/gift-cards-survey/\n\nFrom the cited pages: 43% of U.S. adults have at least one unused gift card, voucher or store credit, about $27 billion in outstanding value; the average amount per person is $244 and the median is $100; Gen Z adults average $142; Bankrate's analyst said stores such as Walmart and Starbucks have more than $1 billion in unused gift cards on their books. Our math: $27 billion / $244 = about 111 million people; $27 billion / a made-up 5 dollar coffee = 5.4 billion coffees. These are survey estimates from 2024. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #giftcards #money #howtheymakemoney",
